<title>UK: NWE jet fuel prices firmer but premiums softer.</title>
<headline>NWE jet fuel prices firmer but premiums softer.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE jet fuel oil prices firmed $1-2 per tonne but the full effects of a price rise in line with firmer benchmark gas oil futures were countered by slightly weaker premiums as buyers stayed scarce and supplies long, traders said.</p>
<p>Prompt lifting barge premiums slipped 50 cents to talk around July IPE +$14/+$15 fob ARA with cargoes valued around $19 over the July IPE gas oil contract cif NWE.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7456</p>
